macOS: bind notification completion to an atomic journal serial and phase.

Cider-Topic: sync/msync
Cider-Requires: 0104-msync-thread-local-fork-admission.patch
Cider-Status: nondefault alternative excluding0105-0108; matching magic5 pair required
Cider-Review-By: independent scoped memory-order/lifetime/death/fork review and parent
Cider-Test: exact-header thread/process recovery, stale helpers, live stopped owner,
 notification scope and serial bound; five negative header variants rejected

Preserve the F8 global owner, independent death lease,16-byte state slots,
thread epochs, native frame pins, Mach/ulock waits and atomic WaitAll decision.
COMMITTED remains the decision point. An applied journal is cleared only AFTER
actual notification callbacks, using exact serial+phase CAS. A stale helper may
send advisory duplicate wakes but cannot clear a newer serial or replay old data.

The committer snapshots its own completed journal while still owning the gate,
then leaves, notifies synchronously, and retires that exact tag without another
owner acquisition. Recovery retains admission/fd/token refresh and owner-held
CLEAN entry. Finish consumes its guard and completes its own notifications;
a later journal may already be pending. All ten production callers obey this.

Shared magic advances to5. Commit serials fail before2^62 wrap instead of2^64;
no semaphore counts or API results are clamped/faked. The new tag CAS and possible
duplicate callbacks have a measured cost to establish; no performance or overall
M1/native-Windows/game acceptance follows from source or native fixtures alone.

